# This CITATION.cff file makes NTLSN citable as a software/data output.
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from it, and Zenodo reads it
# when minting a DOI for a tagged release.
# Format reference: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use NTLSN — the platform, its open datasets, or its methodology —
  please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: "NTLSN — National Teaching and Learning Sector Network"
abstract: >-
  A free, open national commons mapping the Australian higher-education
  teaching and learning sector: events, symposia and professional development
  across all 43 universities; the rescued ALTC/OLT archive of 1,431 funded
  works; the SoTL Index and its DORA-aligned, describe-don't-rank methodology;
  a national library remote-access map; and CORS-open datasets, calendar and
  RSS feeds, and a machine-readable endpoint. Free at the point of use.
authors:
  - family-names: Dianati
    given-names: Seb
    affiliation: "University of Southern Queensland"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dian0007-cloud/ntlsn"
url: "https://ntlsn.com"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-05
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21815413
    description: >-
      Zenodo archive of NTLSN v1.0.0. Zenodo also mints a concept DOI that
      always resolves to the latest version; cite that one when you mean
      "NTLSN" rather than this specific release.
keywords:
  - scholarship of teaching and learning
  - SoTL
  - higher education
  - Australia
  - academic development
  - open educational resources
  - open infrastructure
  - teaching recognition
license: MIT
# The MIT licence above covers the source code. Data and methodology are
# CC BY 4.0 and written content CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, with First Nations ICIP
# excluded from every licence grant — see LICENSE and icip.html for the
# tiered licensing position and docs/licensing-rationale.md for the record.
